# David Kinder's Unicode test prints the Unicode table the game
# carries and then reads characters until escape.
#
# A typed character has to have a ZSCII code (Spec §10.7): the default
# extra characters table covers Latin-1, and this game's own Zcharacter
# table adds ©, ™, and €. Anything else, such as Ē, Ϟ, я, or ڿ from the
# blocks the game prints, is as if it had not been typed, and leaves
# nothing to record, so it is not tried here.

! SEED=1
! GAME=zcode-checkers/unicode-r1.z5

# Basic Latin
x
# Latin-1 Supplement, from the default extra characters table
À
# The Euro sign, from this game's own table
€
<escape>
